{"parentUuid":"aceed086-9e74-4bce-a199-a045fe57b96a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgb1DMoTJADboW4jLkdCu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The real Gemma demo is live and working.\n\n**What's deployed:**\n- **Website** (https://ward-w8cd.onrender.com): when a visitor's check finishes, a \"Try the close read with Gemma\" card appears, in English and Urdu, with a \"Read it with Gemma (demo)\" button. It says plainly that this sends the chat to Ward's demo server and to use the example chat. Real installs of Ward never show it.\n- **Relay** on the bot service (`ward-discord.onrender.com/gemma`): it calls Gemma on Google AI Studio with your key, which stays server-side. It picked **Gemma 4 31B**.\n  - **Other websites refused:** a request from any other site gets a 403, which I checked.\n  - **Rate-limited:** small requests only, 40 per visitor every 10 minutes.\n  - **Nothing kept:** no text is logged and nothing is stored.\n  - **Two fixes:** it now sends back only Gemma's answer, not its thinking, and retries once when Google returns a server error.\n\n**End-to-end test:** I ran Ward's own engine against the live relay, using the same reader and the same requests the website sends. Gemma read the whole example chat with context:\n- **Verdict:** \"urgent\", the correct reading for this chat.\n- **Notes in plain words,** for example \"Calls Ayesha a buffalo to mock their weight\" and \"Suggests removing Ayesha from the group.\"\n- **Zara, who stood up for Ayesha, wasn't flagged.**\n\n**Not tested:** the button itself in a browser. The browser pane here blocks requests to the relay's second address, so I tested the same code path from Node instead. Clicking it in your own browser will confirm it.\n\n**Speed:** that read took about **2 minutes** for 16 messages. The 31B model is large and thinks before answering, and the page shows progress while it works. Your key also has a second Gemma model, likely a faster one. Switching is one Render setting (`GEMMA_MODEL`), and I'd check it reads the example chat just as well before swapping."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_read_input_tokens":946181,"output_tokens":681,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":745,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":946181,"cache_creation_input_tokens":745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":745},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d23cdc7d-f613-42ff-a177-bf8449b97cdf","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgb1DMDjbzbiw228JqvVK","requestRef":"8cd28c09-dc8c-47a8-b486-6ec222b6f725","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"bfb96ece-13ae-4695-8bcb-95a8572d273b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:12:59.490Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"low","perTurnEffort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/haider/Desktop/Hacktoberfest 26/ward","sessionId":"0cf62ca5-911b-48de-86c0-63490519bbda","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"federated-questing-pine"}
