{"parentUuid":"93a6b070-c1dd-4d2f-9202-7d539b5b3535","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgbGdJszwZ8jvAjTyVxsy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: **Ward 0.1.0 (preview)** is up on GitHub Releases.\n\nNext is the **DigitalOcean GPU run**, if you're happy to spend about $2 of your $3.71 credit:\n\n1. I create one RTX 4000 Ada GPU droplet at $0.76/hour.\n2. It installs Ollama, downloads Gemma 4 E4B and E2B, and clones Ward.\n3. It re-runs the scorecard and the red-team set with Gemma, the rows the audit flagged as stale.\n4. I copy the results back into the repo, update the README and REDTEAM tables, and **destroy the droplet**, in about 2 to 2.5 hours in total.\n\nTo keep the spend safe:\n- The droplet has no public services except SSH with a key.\n- I check it's actually gone at the end, so it can't keep billing.\n- I'll stop early if the run is heading past the budget.\n\nNew accounts sometimes need GPU access enabled. If the create is refused, I'll tell you instead of using a pricier size.\n\nSay \"go\" and I'll start it. If you'd rather keep the credit, the next item is the security headers on the Render site."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131,"cache_read_input_tokens":953572,"output_tokens":418,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":33},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":131,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":418,"cache_read_input_tokens":953572,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":131},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverCl